{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: sized containers, packages, balls and blocks",
  "description": "About 45 lines (pipeline fixtures mostly) count a container or piece the catalog can't weigh. \
Parser/reader cases: \"1 750-ml bottle dry white wine\" / \"red wine\" (read as 750 ml), \"1 five-pound leg of lamb\" x3 (spelled-out leading weight), \"1 12- ounce beer\", \"10 -to-12-ounce bag semisweet chocolate chips\" (the parser split a \"10- to 12-ounce\" range), \"1 kabocha squash, roughly 2.5 - 3 pounds\" (weight in the item), \"10 inch flour tortillas\" (an inch size read as the unit), \"1 packet powdered gelatin\" noted \".25 oz\" and \"1 package chocolate wafer cookies\" noted \"9 oz.\" (a weight in the note with a leading dot / no 'ounce' word). \
Cited-weight cases: balls (\"1 ball no-knead pizza dough\" x5, \"1 ball pizza dough\", \"1 ball burrata\", \"1 ball fresh mozzarella\"), blocks (\"1/2 block cream cheese\": 8 oz, \"block konnyaku\"), mixes (\"1 envelope taco seasoning\", \"1 envelope brown gravy mix\", \"1 package ranch mix\", \"1 package instant ramen noodles\"), \"1 small can baby corn\", \"1 small jar roasted red peppers\", \"1 jar furikake\" x2, \"2 container petite-creme yogurt\", bunches and bundles (\"1 bundle scallions\" x5 incl. green onion: a bundle is a bunch; \"1 large bunch basil\", \"2 large bunch rosemary\", \"3 large stalk rosemary\", \"2-3 bunch dried somen\"), \"2 stick rhubarb\", \"1 fillet anchovy\", \"2 wedge lemon\", \"6 leaf nappa cabbage\", \"1 small head napa cabbage\", loaves without a sourced loaf weight (\"1 loaf bread\", \"1 loaf unsliced white bread\", \"6 loaf pita bread\" which means pitas), cinnamon/cassia and kombu 2-inch pieces (cinnamon is trace; kombu needs a per-inch weight). \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora) and, once blocked-ingredient-burndown-from-prod lands, the prod report; make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
